A safe authentication and credential-handling upgrade has been implemented for DelaAI based on the security review recommendations:
Key Upgrades Implemented
Removed Hardcoded Demo Secrets & Defaults:
Purged all fallback dummy keys (DEMO_DELTA_INDIA_KEY) and sample contacts across the client and server.
Credentials are not echoed in plaintext or stored with insecure fallbacks.
Explicit Offline HMAC-SHA256 Signature Diagnostic:
Refactored /api/delta/signature-test to explicitly return diagnosticType: 'LOCAL_HMAC_OFFLINE_GENERATION' and verifiedOnExchange: false.
Returns masked keys (****<last4>) and prominent disclaimers explaining that it computes an offline cryptographic HMAC digest and does not verify authentication against Delta Exchange India servers.
Updated the Settings modal UI to label the diagnostic as an offline HMAC test.
Session Token Management & Authentication Middleware:
Added SessionTokenManager in /src/server/security.ts using constant-time HMAC comparison (crypto.timingSafeEqual) and cryptographic expiration.
Exposed GET /api/auth/session to provide authenticated session tokens to the client.
Secured sensitive endpoints (/api/delta/order, /api/delta/close-position, /api/delta/kill-switch, /api/delta/auto-hedge, /api/delta/signature-test) with sessionManager.authMiddleware().
Strict Input Validation & Sanitization:
Validated order payloads against an allowed symbol whitelist (BTCUSD, BTCUSDT, ETHUSD, etc.), strict positive contract sizes (max 1,000 contracts), valid leverage (1–100), and mandatory limit prices on LIMIT orders.
Validated diagnostic and execution payloads, rejecting malformed requests with structured HTTP 400 errors.
Token Bucket Rate Limiting:
Implemented an in-memory sliding-window token bucket limiter:
Local signature testing: 12 req/min.
Order execution pad / position controls: 30 req/min.
General portfolio queries: 120 req/min.
Returns HTTP 429 with Retry-After headers upon threshold breach.
Automated Secret & Token Redaction:
Added deep secret redaction interceptors (maskSecret, redactSecrets) to Express error handling and terminal logging.
Keys matching patterns for apiSecret, apiKey, token, password, and Bearer tokens are masked or stripped from logs and error payloads.
Strict Paper vs. Live Execution Boundary:
Client requests with mode: "LIVE" are rejected with HTTP 403 (LIVE_TRADING_GATE_LOCKED) unless the server environment variable DELTA_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED="true" is set.
If enabled without server-side credentials, the server returns HTTP 501 (LIVE_EXCHANGE_CREDENTIALS_MISSING).
Removed client-side mock simulation of live orders so unverified live trading cannot be invented or misrepresented.
Verification & Test Suite
Created tests/security_auth.test.ts and registered npm run test in package.json.
All 30/30 security unit tests pass:
Redaction of sensitive fields and bearer tokens.
Cryptographic HMAC-SHA256 signature correctness and offline disclaimer verification.
Input boundary enforcement (symbols, sides, sizes, limit prices).
Rate limiting and cooldown responses.
Session token verification, expiration, and tamper detection.
Paper vs. live boundary gating.
Verified TypeScript compilation (npm run lint / tsc --noEmit) and production bundle build (npm run build).
