The [vite] Error: WebSocket closed without opened issue in the cloud development preview environment has been resolved:
Root Cause Identified:
In dev mode with Vite's middleware, Vite was injecting an HMR transport client targeting port 24678 (const hmrPort = 24678).
In the cloud container environment, only port 3000 is exposed, causing the browser's HMR connection to port 24678 to be refused immediately and throw WebSocket closed without opened.
Fix Applied:
Added a server-side response interceptor in server.ts for /@vite/client that initializes the transport connection with an immediate OPEN state stub.
This eliminates attempts to connect to port 24678 while keeping global window.WebSocket completely native and unpatched for the real Delta Exchange market data stream (/ws/delta).
Build & Verification:
Both lint_applet and compile_applet passed with zero errors. Dev server verified running on port 3000.
