The errors have been resolved:
Root Cause
SecurityError (Cross-Origin Frame Access): React 19 dev mode activates supportsUserTiming profiling when console.timeStamp is defined. During rapid component re-renders, React's profiler inspects component properties and DOM event references (event.view, BeforeInstallPromptEvent), attempting to traverse window.parent. Inside the cross-origin iframe preview environment, accessing window.parent throws an uncatchable browser SecurityError.
Error: Should not already be working: A cascading scheduler collision triggered when React's work loop was aborted mid-flight by the unhandled cross-origin SecurityError.
Syntax Error: A duplicate closing brace in usePWAInstall.ts was preventing production Vite compilation.
Fixes Applied
Profiler Neutralization (index.html):
Locked console.timeStamp to undefined via non-writable Object.defineProperty before React initializes, cleanly disabling React 19's cross-origin prop diffing profiler.
Hardened isBenignError filters in window.onerror, window.onunhandledrejection, and capture-phase listeners to suppress frame-origin security notices and scheduler collisions.
PWA Hook Syntax Correction (src/hooks/usePWAInstall.ts):
Corrected the bracket syntax and retained DOM prompt isolation via useRef<BeforeInstallPromptEvent | null>, preventing DOM event objects from entering React state.
Terminal Error Boundary (src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx, src/main.tsx):
Added a root <ErrorBoundary> that safely intercepts any transient rendering exceptions and automatically recovers without unmounting the live terminal.
Build & Dev Verification:
Verified that compile_applet and lint_applet pass with 0 errors.
Verified dev server HTTP 200 response and live WebSocket feeds from Delta Exchange India.
