Root Cause Analysis
The "Maximum update depth exceeded" error was caused by a cascading dependency loop across three components:
Unstable Audio Callbacks in useSoundEffects:
The audio trigger functions (playTone, playTradeFill, playAlert) in useSoundEffects were plain unmemoized functions. Every render generated brand new function references, which in turn recreated addNotification in App.tsx on every frame.
Unthrottled Auto Pilot Dispatcher in useSniperScalpingEngine:
isAutoSniperEnabled was defaulted to true. Because onSendNotification was being recreated on each frame, executeSniperTrade changed identity on every render. The Auto Pilot Dispatcher effect (useEffect) re-fired immediately, calling executeSniperTrade and triggering state updates in a tight loop.
Feedback Loop in useOptionsStrategyEngine:
The position monitoring effect was calling setActivePosition(updatedPos) unconditionally on every price tick and render, which in turn re-triggered the initialization and monitoring effects because onSendNotification and addAuditLog were in the dependency array.
Key Fixes Applied
Stabilized Sound Effect Callbacks (src/hooks/useSoundEffects.ts):
Wrapped playTone, playTradeFill, playAlert, playKillSwitch, and playFlashBeep in useCallback to guarantee referential stability across all parent renders.
Hardened Auto-Sniper Execution & Cooldown (src/hooks/useSniperScalpingEngine.ts):
Defaulted isAutoSniperEnabled to false (standby mode), requiring intentional activation.
Added lastAttemptTsRef timestamp protection to ensure automatic trade execution can never trigger more than once per 60-second window, even if an order execution fails or is rejected by the risk protection layer.
Stabilized effect dependencies by tracking specific primitive signal values (currentSignal.confidence, currentSignal.riskChecks.tradeApproved) rather than whole-object instances.
Stabilized Options Position Monitoring (src/hooks/useOptionsStrategyEngine.ts):
Added prevMarkPriceRef threshold guarding (< $0.05 tick filter) so position Greeks and premiums are only recomputed on actual underlying market movements.
Converted setActivePosition to a functional state updater setActivePosition((prev) => ...) so activePosition is no longer a dependency of the monitoring effect.
Stored notification and audit log callbacks in refs (onSendNotificationRef, addAuditLogRef), eliminating re-renders caused by callback propagation.
Stabilized Strategy Engine Callbacks (src/components/StrategyEngine.tsx):
Replaced the inline callback onClosePosition: async () => {} with a memoized useCallback.
