The errors have been resolved:
Cause of the Errors
Rate Limiting on Position Closure: /api/delta/close-position was previously bound to the restrictive orderLimiter (30 requests/minute shared across all order placements). When multiple close triggers or automated protective trailing stops fired, the endpoint returned a 429 RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED error ("Rate limit exceeded for close position. Please retry in 40 seconds").
Uncaught Asynchronous Exceptions & Failed Fetch: In PositionsTable.tsx, handleClose invoked await onClosePosition(posId) without a catch block. Network interruptions or non-200 responses caused an unhandled rejection (TypeError: Failed to fetch and rate limit errors) to bubble up to the browser window.
Non-Idempotent Position Lookup: If a position was already closed by a stop loss, take profit, or kill switch, /api/delta/close-position returned a 404 error instead of an idempotent acknowledgment.
Changes Made
Dedicated Position Close Rate Limiter (server.ts):
Replaced the strict 30-req limit on /api/delta/close-position with a dedicated positionCloseLimiter (300 requests/minute) and emergencyKillLimiter (120 requests/minute).
Made /api/delta/close-position idempotent: if a position is already closed or inactive, the server safely responds with { status: 'success', alreadyClosed: true } without throwing a 404.
Robust Client-Side Error & Fallback Handling (App.tsx):
Added comprehensive try / catch blocks to handleClosePosition and handleAutoHedge.
In Paper mode, positions are closed optimistically in local state, restoring available balance and recording closed trade history immediately even if the network or server call experiences delay.
Non-critical errors now display non-blocking notification banners rather than crashing execution.
Safe Async Execution in UI (PositionsTable.tsx):
Added error handling inside handleClose and handleHedge to ensure the closing loader state resets cleanly and promise rejections never bubble up uncaught.
